# Baseline JVM flags for the detokenization service (S9.1).
#
# Not a straw man: this is what a service ships with when nobody has looked at it yet. G1 is on
# (it is the default), the heap is a reasonable fixed size, and there is no pause-time goal.
# The point of the comparison is that "generous but unfocused" is exactly what produces tail
# outliers -- the p50 looks fine either way.

JAVA_OPTS="-Xms2g -Xmx2g \
-XX:+UseG1GC \
-Xlog:gc*,safepoint:file=/var/log/pts/gc-baseline.log:t,uptime,level,tags"
